The bug: `if symbols and len(symbols) != self.ring.ngens: raise ... else: symbols = self.ring.symbols`. The else branch runs even when symbols were passed correctly, overwriting them. Fix: only use self.ring.symbols when symbols not provided.

Minimal fix:

```python
def as_expr(self, *symbols):
    if symbols and len(symbols) != self.ring.ngens:
        raise ValueError("not enough symbols, expected %s got %s" % (self.ring.ngens, len(symbols)))
    if not symbols:
        symbols = self.ring.symbols

    return expr_from_dict(self.as_expr_dict(), *symbols)
```

